course: dictionary
lesson: 4176
title: A godparent is a special adult friend
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have a special meaning in one part of life. The context, meaning the words and sentences around the word, helps you find it. «Christian families often choose godparents, who promise at the baptism to help care for a child.» Here a godparent is a person chosen to make promises at a baptism and to help look after the child.
explain: The clues tell you more. A godmother is a woman and a godfather is a man. Godparents are chosen by the family, and they stay a special adult friend through life. «Godparents are treated almost as family.» So a godparent is not just a guest at a party. They are close to the child.
explain: The same word can mean something different in a story. «In fairy tales, a fairy godmother grants wishes.» The word fairy tells you this godmother is make-believe, a magic helper. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A godparent is a person chosen by a child's family to help them grow up and to be a special adult friend through life.
fact: A godmother is a woman godparent, and a godfather is a man godparent.
fact: At a baptism, godparents promise to help the child grow up in the Christian faith.
fact: Godparents often send birthday presents, come to big events and give advice.
fact: A fairy godmother is a magic helper in fairy tales, such as Cinderella, who grants wishes.
exercise: «Christian families often choose godparents, who promise at the baptism to help care for a child.» What is a godparent? | A teacher who runs a school club | *A person chosen to make promises at a child's baptism and help care for them | A doctor who looks after babies in hospital
exercise: A woman godparent is called a | godchild | godfather | *godmother
exercise: In a fairy tale, what does a fairy godmother do? | Cooks dinner for the king | Sends letters to the school | *Grants wishes like magic
test: «At a baptism the parents and godparents promise, in front of the whole church, to bring the baby up in the faith.» Who makes this promise along with the parents? | the postman | *godparents | the neighbours
test: In family life, what do godparents often do? | *Send birthday presents, come to big events and give advice | Mend the roof and cook the meals | Live in a different country and never visit
exam: «Godparents are treated almost as family.» What does this suggest? | *They are close to the child, like family | They have no place in family life at all | They are strangers to the child
